nt :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3d7a176-49a0-5f40-a976-fffa17513013" :question/math-academy-id "q-141158" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The identity matrix ${I}_{2}$ belongs to $T.$\n\nII. For every $A\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha \\cdot A\\in T.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $T$ contains only matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ However, for the identity matrix ${I}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ we have ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}=1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1=0≯0.$ So, ${I}_{2}\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, let $\\alpha =0\\in R$ and $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}\\in T.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\alpha \\cdot A=0\\cdot A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere the sum of the products of columns' entries is $0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 0=0≯0.$ Hence, $0\\cdot A\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7286fe-b6e2-5544-8bc6-86afc6cdb813" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048896 :topic/id #uuid "ca183854-66cd-5b1f-9d29-03785c3216b8" :topic/math-academy-id 861 :topic/title "Introduction to Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc0166e2-c321-59cc-ae9e-b42ad174c401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476077} {:answer/id #uuid "de5974c9-39d6-52a3-ab8f-fc158e6dadf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de5974c9-39d6-52a3-ab8f-fc158e6dadf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476087} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f14ea8b-ad13-5765-8427-d87faeb2ca41" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ded02ba-f54b-5bf2-be08-b697eb7714aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476047} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d17bad-d43a-5dad-8bb4-1b2cc6f5b94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ded02ba-f54b-5bf2-be08-b697eb7714aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476047} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c8b6157-374a-5570-b89d-490ff94af531" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cbc5020-eeb1-5fd1-b4f2-578768f0f9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476054} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb29206-4453-5434-b483-0cbf0dcac87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdb29206-4453-5434-b483-0cbf0dcac87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476099} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0f9172-c39f-5533-9ffb-24079a8c68ae" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0da062ca-289e-5f8c-ab1e-076e2589345a" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $1\\times 3$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nP = \\begin{bmatrix}-0.1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nQ = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nR = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -0.1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $P$ has $1$ row and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 1.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $Q$ has $1$ row and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 3.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $R$ has $3$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 1.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7286fe-b6e2-5544-8bc6-86afc6cdb813" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048896 :topic/id #uuid "ca183854-66cd-5b1f-9d29-03785c3216b8" :topic/math-academy-id 861 :topic/title "Introduction to Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3483822-cd0d-54a3-80b8-e46dc46533cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476066} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d332d9-a454-57b3-a4ed-a3fe3b4c389b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db