5bee-9f3e-2ce798122c9b" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $3\\times 4$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nB = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1.1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1.1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ -3 & \\sqrt{2} & 1.1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2} & -1 & 1.1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -0.1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -0.1 & 7 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -0.1 & 0 & 1.1 & 1.1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $B$ has $3$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 4.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $D$ has $4$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 4.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7286fe-b6e2-5544-8bc6-86afc6cdb813" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048896 :topic/id #uuid "ca183854-66cd-5b1f-9d29-03785c3216b8" :topic/math-academy-id 861 :topic/title "Introduction to Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c68415-4265-5be0-947e-6008712111c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476016} {:answer/id #uuid "cb87c17d-8425-5393-8082-6f916846e5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb87c17d-8425-5393-8082-6f916846e5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476076} :answer-field/id #uuid "4902276e-4658-56ee-b43f-2ce8757057d7" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id 