#uuid "a54ab5f5-3aa4-5cb2-a67f-b05de4913639" :answer-field/key "$B$ is lower triangular." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac6bf26c-daf9-5149-b82c-ecff54a2e1d7" :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $B$ is upper triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular: **False.** This fails because $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because the result of $B-{B}^{T}$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB-{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $B$ is upper triangular." :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576360 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488404} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 20.494 :task-item/id #uuid "125661b8-3de5-48d1-9163-f940bf4c164b" :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "1094c3c3-975f-530e-bff0-7807d9d9ab97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488395} {:answer/id #uuid "52d664dd-84d9-50fd-8032-ee9ee3585001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488399} {:answer/id #uuid "539855fa-6c5d-53c2-8e6b-3ae037750849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488400}] :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571} :task-item/working-ended-at #inst "2026-10-17T23:27:50.880Z"}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049310 :topic/id #uuid "eb6655db-68e9-5ef3-bf7a-81223e92dac0" :topic/math-academy-id 1414 :topic/title "Linear Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf9aace5-3d08-53ff-85ab-200c5a3982c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573983} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb69671-cc06-5f76-af31-30ccd861609f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cb69671-cc06-5f76-af31-30ccd861609f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573984} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bc14490-1b7a-563d-b53d-3186ffc04007" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044ef98f-d831-5243-89bf-3154931941db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573985} {:answer/id #uuid "38499c5b-c09f-5d18-b3e6-81a1edd32874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38499c5b-c09f-5d18-b3e6-81a1edd32874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573986} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a09971-5f2b-5f57-a88a-c2d7c71f351b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573996} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "353bc1c0-2f53-5a5a-b94b-3857873ea7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573987} {:answer/id #uuid "a1710105-4951-5d1f-b992-6c3f9c479587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "353bc1c0-2f53-5a5a-b94b-3857873ea7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573987} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac18f23-f1b4-53a4-97f4-4e3f6c111735" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d18683e-9cdc-5535-b6a1-ea077ac9eff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288426" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $4x+2=4x+2$\n\n- **II.** $-2x-1=-2x-1$\n\n- **III.** $3x+5=3x+9$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & =4x+2 \\\\ 4x+2-4x & =4x+2-4x \\\\ 2 & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $4x+2=4x+2$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-1 & =-2x-1 \\\\ -2x-1+2x & =-2x-1+2x \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-2x-1=-2x-1$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+5 & =3x+9 \\\\ 3x+5-3x & =3x+9-3x \\\\ 5 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049310 :topic/id #uuid "eb6655db-68e9-5ef3-bf7a-81223e92dac0" :topic/math-academy-id 1414 :topic/title "Linear Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1790b83e-7780-5313-99ea-bb10de434617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573989} {:answer/id #uuid "82dbfad8-bf35-55fb-ad22-e76e4b8b9a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573990 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572817 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492056} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82dbfad8-bf35-55fb-ad22-e76e4b8b9a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573990 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572817 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492056} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "b55fd536-3e0e-59f4-8009-976c5f1cf687" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573998} {:answer-fi