s {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "df8ab297-c513-5d93-9250-0c73f1d09739" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc8f5f5a-7e03-528b-a06c-bf3c3858a8c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288431" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3x+4=3x+4$\n\n- **II.** $x-5=x-2$\n\n- **III.** $2x+3=x+3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4 & =3x+4 \\\\ 3x+4-3x & =3x+4-3x \\\\ 4 & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $3x+4=3x+4$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5 & =x-2 \\\\ x-5-x & =x-2-x \\\\ -5 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =x+3 \\\\ 2x+3-x & =x+3-x \\\\ x+3 & =3 \\\\ x+3-3 & =3-3 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x+3=x+3$ has the unique solution $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572817 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492056} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 47.556999999999995 :task-item/id #uuid "d97fb804-bbf3-4242-b4fe-be3b8ddcba76" :task-item/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574008} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "82dbfad8-bf35-55fb-ad22-e76e4b8b9a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573990} {:answer/id #uuid "1dbf8499-dbd8-5276-8885-6ffc17db9e0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573991} {:answer/id #uuid "5108105d-89e2-5b5d-b37e-96caf1ff54ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573993}] :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571} :task-item/working-ended-at #inst "2026-10-17T01:29:03.277Z"}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af735f8-4787-5fc2-9829-e980798699d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493213} {:answer/id #uuid "fc007165-3170-5c92-bfc7-4dba420e35f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc007165-3170-5c92-bfc7-4dba420e35f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493289} :answer-field/id #uuid "30a48790-00a3-595a-b572-1ab265a0b954" :answer-field/key "answer-c2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6517541b-f8ff-51f4-a2a2-34924e88d0a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493222} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd7b3e-5382-5331-b00a-965b7684301d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd7b3e-5382-5331-b00a-965b7684301d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493243} :answer-field/id #uuid "a47d2fd5-ef6c-53aa-8aed-851210680dde" :answer-field/key "answer-c1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493244}] :question/id #uuid "8f368a35-083c-55a1-a2d5-fbfb51cf7f2f" :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 3 (question_59459046).\n\nThe inverse of $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&3\\\\4&5&6\\\\-1&-2&0\\end{bmatrix}$ is the proposed matrix $B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4/3&2/3&1/3\\\\2/3&-1/3&-2/3\\\\1/3&0&1/3\\end{bmatrix}$. Select the true choice(s).\n\nc1. True: {{answer-c1}}\n\nc2. False: {{answer-c2}}" :question/worked-solution "The assertion is true. Exact row-column multiplication gives $AB=BA=I_3$. For example, the first row of AB is $(-4/3+4/3+1, 2/3-2/3, 1/3-4/3+1)=(1,0,0)$; the other rows give $(0,1,0)$ and $(0,0,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0077f4e-bfef-5c44-9c4f-22e790c66054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494118} {:answer/id #uuid "f470c94f-5751-5b47-a030-8985df3f2d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f470c94f-5751-5b47-a030-8985df3f2d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494120} :answer-field/id #uuid "276d5850-899a-5418-b118-58774ff396c5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0427735-f1b6-5953-9a58-65ffe3fc0cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494104} {:answer/id #uuid "d93ba829-e163-58c2-b76e-e291c5f8be1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d93ba829-e163-58c2-b76e-e291c5f8be1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494113} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc47d48-c82a-5502-bb58-b7f089ff6b6b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c3effa8-82fb-5fb4-8d49-078df0fff8cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494098} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb4386c-3ca1-56b1-a1f1-27eda3db5ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbb4386c-3ca1-56b1-a1f1-27eda3db5ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494122} :answer-field/id #uuid "b26b8e2c-d5f7-5d56-ac89-1e186c2dea2a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03ad73f2-dfe8-5b7e-bde4-05067dff734f" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{3y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-5{x}^{2}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-2{x}^{3},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-2{x}^{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2} \\\\  & \\ne -5{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-2{x}^{3}$ and ${y}^{′}=-6{x}^{2}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3y}{x} \\\\ -6{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3(-2{x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ -6{x}^{2} & =-6{x}^{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-2{x}^{3}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4330cfb7-8007-5f4b-b65a-6b8ca9b8b25b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494094} {:answer/id #uuid "8a470ecb-d8a1-5134-bd03-7aa6af28cd48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id 