iginal equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ -10x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2(-5{x}^{2})}{x} \\\\ -10x & =-10x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-5{x}^{2}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494099 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011418b9-1534-59df-abe2-f6a8f8a26db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494074} {:answer/id #uuid "021de50f-ea33-579e-a44c-452e1f743ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021de50f-ea33-579e-a44c-452e1f743ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4d4fa50-0013-5de3-852e-7f4ee29ad547" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea9441a-4d5f-5c20-89eb-3e9b8023d358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494080} {:answer/id #uuid "4b214493-23b3-5f84-b21a-00cd796322e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b214493-23b3-5f84-b21a-00cd796322e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494095} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc1e684f-2d41-5bc0-9ae4-f3a4f678e975" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494110} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9629c86a-b3b2-5321-9f76-9106260891aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494103} {:answer/id #uuid "de177bd4-487f-572f-bd7e-c963cf812a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9629c86a-b3b2-5321-9f76-9106260891aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494103} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd4acafd-7da1-5123-afa5-23235bdb411a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62fb2fb6-fffd-5184-a1c6-901c28207971" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{3y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-3{x}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-6{x}^{2}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-3{x}^{3},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3{x}^{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2} \\\\  & \\ne -6{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-3{x}^{3}$ and ${y}^{′}=-9{x}^{2}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3y}{x} \\\\ -9{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3(-3{x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ -9{x}^{2} & =-9{x}^{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-3{x}^{3}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043bd6b5-f398-59fb-9664-c843c3927785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494128} {:answer/id #uuid "fed93e13-4643-5fa5-adb6-1d03e9aecd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fed93e13-4643-5fa5-adb6-1d03e9aecd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494224} :answer-field/id #uuid "185aa277-ec0b-5b7f-9dfd-7fd410156dfc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "119b6234-2b31-5432-915d-1e7dc0ef6b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494133} {:answer/id #uuid "1cf34b6d-fb8d-5cff-9900-0f2e7b496e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cf34b6d-fb8d-5cff-9900-0f2e7b496e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494138} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dff065e-2b3b-5c1e-a226-f81d326f6baf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63afce1e-e0ab-5d34-81d4-696e5637c1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494168} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8f849b-f988-5a2f-8dc4-21d836414a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63afce1e-e0ab-5d34-81d4-696e5637c1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494168} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f318fe0-a53e-51ad-b079-e7ecb29bbd16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "186f19a6-4a5f-585e-b13e-b8bce737384f" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6 + \\frac{4 y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=- x^{4} - 2 x - 1$\n- **II.** $y=- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1$\n- **III.** $y=2 x^{4} - x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=- x^{4} - 2 x - 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 4 x^{3} - 2.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 + \\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 4 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\cdot \\left(- x^{4} - 2 x - 1\\right)}{x}+6 \\\\ - 4 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}- 4 x^{3} - 2 - \\frac{4}{x} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- x^{4} - 2 x - 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 12 x^{3} - 2.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 + \\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 12 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\cdot \\left(- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1\\right)}{x}+6 \\\\ - 12 x^{3} - 2 & \\overset{?}{=}- 12 x^{3} - 2 + \\frac{4}{x} \\\\ - \\frac{4}{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 3 x^{4} - 2 x + 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 x^{4} - x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8 x^{3} - 1.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 + \\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ 8 x^{3} - 1 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\cdot \\left(2 x^{4} - x\\right)}{x}+6 \\\\ 8 x^{3} - 1 & \\overset{?}{=}8 x^{3} + 2 \\\\ -3 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 x^{4} - x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5779ad75-a9e3-519a-83ec-38ffe7d63e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494164} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c27302-eb79-5e34-ab06-6e23f1c7b0ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4c27302-eb79-5e34-ab06-6e23f1c7b0ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494216} :answer-field/id #uuid "c46a625b-90ba-578a-b81e-66724eae64ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a88c68b-2230-5b15-a29b-58b0cdaf4b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494160} {:answer/id #uuid "beaf076d-0d2e-5e77-94ac-b9ea1cb7b58b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "beaf076d-0d2e-5e77-94ac-b9ea1cb7b58b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494200} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccfd7c37-8011-5662-abf6-925422db5d7c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64aca6ee-096a-51b1-b276-74fc2847b0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494169} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3ece63-d679-5ff6-a15d-e19e115bad5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c3ece63-d679-5ff6-a15d-e19e115bad5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494173} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7b4cfc2-eb9e-534f-acb8-2d15173fb353" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "445c16a9-31b8-52c6-9989-0214ce5be143" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=e^{x} - 1$\n- **II.** $y=- e^{x}$\n- **III.** $y=- e^{- x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=e^{x} - 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(e^{x} - 1\\right) \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}e^{x} - 1 \\\\ 1 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=e^{x} - 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- e^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ - e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- e^{x}\\right) \\\\ - e^{x} & =- e^{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=- e^{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}- e^{- x} \\\\ 2 e^{- x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- e^{- x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054d7925-1847-562b-ae23-d79faab9f29c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494129} {:answer/id #uuid "f09cf4be-e51e-5251-bd38-9ee9d165772c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "054d7925-1847-562b-ae23-d79faab9f29c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494129} :answer-field/id #uuid "02340bc0-0e35-511b-8bdf-634b3b1617f2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8541587a-6f0d-5e4c-8ba8-dffa29013166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494178} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ed4684-cdcb-588c-a840-886c4cff8762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4ed4684-cdcb-588c-a840-886c4cff8762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494189} :answer-field/id #uuid "4066b5b3-5f66-5bb3-98fb-812b6147d21a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e7daa0-d022-513e-8651-4ce1f2aae5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494159} {:answer/id #uuid "60ac3f8d-bd55-5484-966f-7ce2dde8f33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ac3f8d-bd55-5484-966f-7ce2dde8f33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494166} :answer-field/id #uuid "42fde4a2-8a28-5a07-8c04-aafb5c22896f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "482041dd-1ea5-59f6-ae3d-2788e211524d" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=3 e^{x} - 2$\n- **II.** $y=-2 + 3 e^{- x}$\n- **III.** $y=3 e^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=3 e^{x} - 2,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(3 e^{x} - 2\\right) \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2 - 3 e^{x} \\\\ 6 e^{x} - 2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=3 e^{x} - 2$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2 + 3 e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 3 e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ - 3 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(-2 + 3 e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ - 3 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}2 - 3 e^{- x} \\\\ -2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2 + 3 e^{- x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=3 e^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(3 e^{x}\\right) \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}- 3 e^{x} \\\\ 6 e^{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=3 e^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c479766-f0ed-598c-88bb-cd9e4aca3186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494131} {:answer/id #uuid "24634106-6b6d-53e3-8be4-e55502551d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24634106-6b6d-53e3-8be4-e55502551d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494141} :answer-field/id #uuid "043748fe-9f8c-5795-a26b-5e9bffd6a289" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02bc6886-cd38-59b8-accd-e14e1de740aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494126} {:answer/id #uuid "b37f87cf-f5db-55e3-8ba9-32d8700d9e21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02bc6886-cd38-59b8-accd-e14e1de740aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494126} :answer-field/id #uuid "963e2bab-fb7a-5aa3-aa24-bac5aef7a3d5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "473054af-72eb-5f9d-8413-69674dad30c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494157} {:answer/id #uuid "890ac81e-3d06-5feb-9f77-114c33f9cb4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "473054af-72eb-5f9d-8413-69674dad30c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494157} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae8b77b5-7e47-5062-bd24-e3807ebcecfa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7af2ca83-a7d1-5afb-b854-4b08878292b3" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=2 - 2 e^{x}$\n- **II.** $y=e^{x} + 1$\n- **III.** $y=e^{- x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=2 - 2 e^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 2 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ - 2 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(2 - 2 e^{x}\\right) \\\\ - 2 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2 e^{x} - 2 \\\\ 2 - 4 e^{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 - 2 e^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=e^{x} + 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(e^{x} + 1\\right) \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}- e^{x} - 1 \\\\ 2 e^{x} + 1 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=e^{x} + 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ - e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ - e^{- x} & =- e^{- x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=e^{- x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17eda594-9fa2-5642-b504-32094afb3531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494134 :task-item/_response