id #edb/ref 17592186494187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8d10f76-307c-51d4-9770-a45f901a8f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494197} {:answer/id #uuid "fb124e81-c8cd-5031-bf70-fde92df49f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494222 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577104 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494183} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb124e81-c8cd-5031-bf70-fde92df49f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494222 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577104 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494183} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5c30af1-43f6-5328-ad5b-fcc88c1b7c45" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9090ebe8-9264-5307-a4ba-1cdbb63b8aca" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=-2 - e^{- x}$\n- **II.** $y=- 3 e^{- x}$\n- **III.** $y=2 e^{- x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=-2 - e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(-2 - e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}2 + e^{- x} \\\\ -2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2 - e^{- x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 3 e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ 3 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(- 3 e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ 3 e^{- x} & =3 e^{- x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=- 3 e^{- x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 2 e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- y \\\\ - 2 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}-1\\cdot \\left(2 e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ - 2 e^{- x} & =- 2 e^{- x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=2 e^{- x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577104 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494183} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 39.629 :task-item/id #uuid "c94d5cf4-cac2-41a5-af05-bfd26b0b42af" :task-item/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577105} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "17eda594-9fa2-5642-b504-32094afb3531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494134} {:answer/id #uuid "721f2a1c-4389-5465-8089-93e02f836757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494171} {:answer/id #uuid "fb124e81-c8cd-5031-bf70-fde92df49f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident