nswer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494214} :answer-field/id #uuid "a207163e-9b18-5847-88c5-ebf55d302e51" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d5258b-456f-5a33-a2dc-5f200f505556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494180} {:answer/id #uuid "ce760cea-a8a9-5ce0-bc90-55ed5352aeb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce760cea-a8a9-5ce0-bc90-55ed5352aeb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494207} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e8bc87-246a-5ed2-aedc-78f9176e6562" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "adc22bc0-1147-5a29-8060-cd0632ce97e9" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-3 + \\frac{2 y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=- x^{2} + 3 x$\n- **II.** $y=- 3 x^{2} + 4 x$\n- **III.** $y=2 x^{2} + 4 x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=- x^{2} + 3 x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 - 2 x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-3 + \\frac{2 y}{x} \\\\ 3 - 2 x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot \\left(- x^{2} + 3 x\\right)}{x}-3 \\\\ 3 - 2 x & =3 - 2 x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=- x^{2} + 3 x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 3 x^{2} + 4 x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4 - 6 x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-3 + \\frac{2 y}{x} \\\\ 4 - 6 x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot \\left(- 3 x^{2} + 4 x\\right)}{x}-3 \\\\ 4 - 6 x & \\overset{?}{=}5 - 6 x \\\\ -1 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 3 x^{2} + 4 x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 x^{2} + 4 x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4 x + 4.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-3 + \\frac{2 y}{x} \\\\ 4 x + 4 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot \\left(2 x^{2} + 4 x\\right)}{x}-3 \\\\ 4 x + 4 & \\overset{?}{=}4 x + 5 \\\\ -1 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 x^{2} + 4 x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3284c12a-285e-5b37-b1d3-d2b54e875d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494146} {:answer/id #uuid "d65aeea0-320d-5e02-9c26-f420ce319205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d65aeea0-320d-5e02-9c26-f420ce319205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494209} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dad1ea5-f432-5bca-8f9b-610fc52026cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61d8db18-1a08-588a-909e-dad6d5502ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494167} {:answer/id #uuid "e33d712a-5c46-537e-a67c-313162b8c8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61d8db18-1a08-588a-909e-dad6d5502ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494167} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d1c65e-13db-53aa-a02c-2265851c694c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494145} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a78be4a0-8c73-516f-970a-3c49bbd3d29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494190} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf2ea96-a3e9-5044-91ff-48b24bff7f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a78be4a0-8c73-516f-970a-3c49bbd3d29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494190} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f289b0-c3c5-521f-85b6-09ac6cef5f84" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bc2cf9f7-3ebb-510f-a50d-009e8d3e2d2f" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$\n- **II.** $y=1 - 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$\n- **III.** $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=1 - 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- \\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(1 - 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{- \\frac{1}{2}}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(x\\right)} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2 x}{e^{\\frac{1}{2}}} \\\\ - \\frac{2 x}{e^{\\frac{1}{2}}} - \\frac{2}{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=1 - 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2587e0fd-c2da-505a-bf9d-cc93290c0ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494142} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b343bc-0484-5d70-a0c5-1ddd2b18072d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2587e0fd-c2da-505a-bf9d-cc93290c0ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494142} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a713518-e004-530d-9096-230f529b44ea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096d33a3-6dda-5eca-9787-1267117dc021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494130} {:answer/id #uuid "b852ee82-598a-5919-bab9-78ffe8c60820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b852ee82-598a-5919-bab9-78ffe8c60820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494196} :answer-field/id #uuid "44ec42b0-3682-544b-ac01-636f3d9ba276" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e3ca188-d290-5b7c-b166-6a82a6e35286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494165} {:answer/id #uuid "90017a13-d869-5d7f-8dcc-9db9f9847434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90017a13-d869-5d7f-8dcc-9db9f9847434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494182} :answer-field/id #uuid "d92d36ab-20e8-59a2-ace3-8d51ed597e85" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dbaa0cb0-f596-5793-b9d2-327ba3dab2cf" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1$\n- **II.** $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$\n- **III.** $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- \\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right)} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(x\\right)} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2 x e^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\ - 2 x e^{\\frac{1}{2}} - \\frac{2}{x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}2e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d4411e8-b0c5-5fd9-83d7-340374341d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494152} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc695d9-9b09-53cb-b2c8-0e2fcebe2241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dc695d9-9b09-53cb-b2c8-0e2fcebe2241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494186} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e15a5f6-e840-50a0-bee6-957bd3690a66" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e17fc39-ce4e-5f23-aef2-7d4f4a32cce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494132} {:answer/id #uuid "30edde06-8d14-519f-b9a8-6edf3a1c7d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e17fc39-ce4e-5f23-aef2-7d4f4a32cce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494132} :answer-field/id #uuid "b026a76d-9219-51e6-be00-745e96ad4566" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54e193b0-efba-5f1d-9e44-cf90148ec585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494163} {:answer/id #uuid "87b240b2-46b1-512a-bdf2-b9fd61e0a69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e193b0-efba-5f1d-9e44-cf90148ec585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494163} :answer-field/id #uuid "de72884f-8c58-5c74-aa9c-e35bf2e4d062" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed22e244-8467-5b30-9a78-06a03f1761ac" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$\n- **II.** $y=3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$\n- **III.** $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{3}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\left(3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{3}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{3}{x} & =\\frac{3}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3 e^{\\frac{1}{3}}}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{1}{3}}}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3db4e6c-ec76-5c68-b9ea-8a870249452d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494208} {:answer/id #uuid "eedafe67-a61c-5e88-8cb0-53e032a87451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3db4e6c-ec76-5c68-b9ea-8a870249452d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494208} :answer-field/id #uuid "3621bd74-a8f3-532e-93ba-8265ce22c897" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494148} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "807d73f1-95c3-5598-b78d-c5c37b01ff37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494177} {:answer/id #uuid "f380cb57-bb9a-55b5-8bb7-5942f0098316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f380cb57-bb9a-55b5-8bb7-5942f0098316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494221} :answer-field/id #uuid "c64eae15-0d0b-5d44-aa93-8afc1cfa5199" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52571d72-0344-521b-acf7-3b8804ca0284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494162} {:answer/id #uuid "67f09018-86bc-53cd-a196-213802abc706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52571d72-0344-521b-acf7-3b8804ca0284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494162} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcf53b2e-9588-5276-aeec-2aee943daafe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f13e106a-779d-594b-9ac2-fa322d45064e" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=3 e^{x} + 1$\n- **II.** $y=- 2 e^{- x}$\n- **III.** $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=3 e^{x} + 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(3 e^{x} + 1\\right) \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3 e^{x} + 1 \\\\ -1 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=3 e^{x} + 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 2 e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2 e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ 2 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- 2 e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ 2 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}- 2 e^{- x} \\\\ 4 e^{- x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 2 e^{- x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 3 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ - 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- 3 e^{x} - 2\\right) \\\\ - 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}- 3 e^{x} - 2 \\\\ 2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e41394-7b55-5bc3-bc16-70da08ee175b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496602} {:answer/id #uuid "b143c46e-de12-5d3b-b2c3-3361fcf67088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19e41394-7b55-5bc3-bc16-70da08ee175b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496602} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd8616f4-9a95-592a-b132-b5ee4d8121c7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496631} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021d0e53-551b-5043-b015-a6c429c20350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496592} {:answer/id #uuid "0e51cf2a-f44d-50be-b8c8-f0f53e11215b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021d0e53-551b-5043-b015-a6c429c20350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496592} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7f50105-bf2d-5f42-8541-d2897e8819e0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496636} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ba86b24-a09e-58ef-a131-22bb7e0d8b2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496609} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa8b251-d22b-5c20-85ca-0282eba2a1bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aa8b251-d22b-5c20-85ca-0282eba2a1bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496622} :answer-field/id #uuid "e01ef92e-e0ac-5a62-9cc8-729882dff28c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04cab1c1-b4c4-563e-a4e0-aea26627ab39" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(5+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}-2y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(3)=2$\n- **II.** $(4+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}-3y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(3)=4$\n- **III.** $(5+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{d^3y}{dx^3}-3y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(3)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=-1,\\,{y}^{″}(3)=0$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(5+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}-2y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x}$ together with the initial condition $y(3)=2.$\n\n- System II is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(4+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}-3y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x}$ together with the initial condition $y(3)=4.$\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation $(5+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{d^3y}{dx^3}-3y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x}$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(3)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=-1,\\,{y}^{″}(3)=0.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "093ce5ea-7ce2-5813-a68f-45ee253e563a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496598} {:answer/id #uuid "9248089b-449f-5a57-9d31-012fd4df93ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9248089b-449f-5a57-9d31-012fd4df93ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496621} :answer-field/id #uuid "68f91a6e-36ba-5b8e-a47c-cc852cf6015b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b42851-445f-5a9d-ab02-aa2985e5a712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496599} {:answer/id #uuid "dac405a2-0857-5f8a-aa9b-a6e0e1bf8e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :an