n $(5+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}-5y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x}$ together with the initial condition $y(4)=5.$\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. We have here a second-order ordinary differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc5bab6c-1ce7-58b5-a59d-cff2ce35ecca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049715 :topic/id #uuid "0d3ad89a-14be-5528-a12e-4252d281243e" :topic/math-academy-id 1103 :topic/title "Parallel Vectors"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89e26bbe-a817-539a-b5c9-be6506c0db3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504926} {:answer/id #uuid "a83fa579-2e1c-5c9c-a54f-fb39b0fb170f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a83fa579-2e1c-5c9c-a54f-fb39b0fb170f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504944} :answer-field/id #uuid "750744fa-4268-560c-94aa-bcda09a12b5d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504913} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c83165b-d5fd-5aef-92a0-c8953312f526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504939} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6c6cd2-265c-56c1-a5d2-8e030d0852f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec6c6cd2-265c-56c1-a5d2-8e030d0852f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504993} :answer-field/id #uuid "83abf799-8401-5836-9882-3ea1ecdfd3be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504922} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f8d53c-5032-5c11-9c9a-b33ceb62c4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504850} {:answer/id #uuid "1d31e534-5f72-58c4-ae68-136d090f729b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d31e534-5f72-58c4-ae68-136d090f729b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504864} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9864a53-620b-5536-9bb8-09d9ede26c66" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1bac862a-89e7-5ff0-8707-8ba70047c178" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae3cb3c0a30251ff66193040df7d2f564e771ba60ec711c915099ee2056bfcb5.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $b =-2e$\n- **II.** $c =-d$\n- **III.** $b = 2e$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $b$ and $e$ have the same direction. So, $b\\neq-2e$.\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $c$ and $d$ have the same direction. So, $c\\neq-d$.\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $e$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $b$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $b=2e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."} {:db/id 