wer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512005} :answer-field/id #uuid "fee93e3b-06c8-5ee1-8dd8-365bfe5b8c36" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ce2ea85-552c-5e62-a3ef-0a5e7f4819be" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=n\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\n\n- Statement II is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\pi+2n\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049091 :topic/id #uuid "d9b41e19-22fc-5fad-93ae-b8f50010d70b" :topic/math-academy-id 3557 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80ec998e-ebc7-57cf-9585-e7037333b8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db