rvals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nI. $x\\in (-2,0]$\n\nII. $x\\in [0,3]$\n\nIII. $x\\in [-1,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- On interval I, $x\\in (-2,0]$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval II, $x\\in [0,3]$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval III, $x\\in [-1,3]$, the function is **not** invertible. Some horizontal lines will intersect the restricted graph more than once.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f524ac8-715f-5cd9-8794-f271f909a7a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513064} {:answer/id #uuid "b16a857a-a6c8-518b-a59c-8ddefbc35585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b16a857a-a6c8-518b-a59c-8ddefbc35585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218651307