fa86-486e-5d5d-b4b0-4cf53a93a9be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc80ab4d-3d7a-55d7-91ad-7a0e0bb91f1b" :question/problem "![](images/62/62233fc5bc77f34837790174b42f6bf3652bfbc55fbd031b3881d072f0cd2475.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nI. $x\\in [-2,0]$\n\nII. $x\\in [0,3)$\n\nIII. $x\\in [-1,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- On interval I, $x\\in [-2,0]$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval II, $x\\in [0,3)$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval III, $x\\in [-1,3]$, the function is **not** invertible. Some horizontal lines will intersect the restricted graph more than once.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513099 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "708a0bd6-cff7-58a7-b12b-8c2c6f7c6ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513125} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4818e9-ffff-5320-97a4-36bafb40f059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd4818e9-ffff-5320-97a4-36bafb40f059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513155} :answer-field/id #uuid "3622d97b-5226-58d5-9e67-20ff43def90b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07081e6b-5b48-5d7b-aa0c-02968b5e3cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513092} {:answer/id #uuid "be6ec870-3dfa-56bb-b0b4-3883abd44faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07081e6b-5b48-5d7b-aa0c-02968b5e3cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513092} :answer-field/id #uuid "782bd375-c93d-57f5-8f10-be0ed56a5688" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4018637c-4a24-5b0c-bf7e-2e205ebfcfc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513109} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc0fcfd-f37f-507d-98b7-2dad7d622ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fc0fcfd-f37f-507d-98b7-2dad7d622ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513124} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ecbea19-3904-5869-b505-897eb359bebe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7917315-c958-5df7-8510-bfc839d206ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513153} {:answer/id #uuid "e991b944-6495-527a-b9e0-73d1685aa00e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7917315-c958-5df7-8510-bfc839d206ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513153} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6cd450f-9f38-5284-8c92-4bc5fb914be0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15af3203-5ba4-5a70-ae42-f31ddb49ea15" :question/problem "![](images/fc/fc809b4528a9c050e3b7579a867b586178da0e296cc213343b9d4882a74fd038.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nEach graph shows its entire domain; an open circle excludes its endpoint.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nGraph positions: **I.** upper left; **II.** upper right; **III.** lower left; **IV.** lower right." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/22/22ba710ce7df0493a50795f555ed98ba49abf19fe5668e9734c63412aaeeeceb.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that:\n\n- For graphs II, III, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, these graphs show one-to-one functions. As a result, these functions are invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, IV, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. These are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."}]
